From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:58:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(items): translate Java overrides and book data

Apply mapped potion, instrument, and block-state overrides as Java 26.3 components. Preserve Bedrock book pages and metadata, and retain the enchantment glint for an empty enchantment list so item presentation survives translation.

Translate Bedrock chargedItem into Java charged_projectiles through the
shared item converter. Preserve the authoritative arrow or rocket stack,
including auxiliary and nested data, and clear unloaded charges. Restrict
nested conversion to vanilla ammunition so a charged crossbow cannot
recursively contain another charged crossbow.

Isolated official BDS 1.26.51.1 build 51061372, protocol 2193, supplies one
charged arrow, retains auxiliary value 15 for a tipped arrow, and loads a
rocket from the offhand with its Fireworks tag. Rockets elsewhere in the
inventory do not load in this controlled probe. Java and ViaProxy live
charge and firing timing remain unverified; captures stay private.

Preserve rocket Flight as an unsigned byte and all star/explosion fields
in standard Java fireworks components. Use the target native palette and
purple invalid/empty-color fallback, retaining shape, fade order, trail
and flicker. Native readers accept only byte fields and byte arrays;
wrong types retain native defaults. Missing flight is zero, not one.

Official BDS 1.26.51.1 build 51061372 supplies all 16 creative star colors
and the rocket/explosion NBT shape. Focused inspection of the matching
Windows binary confirms typed fields, unsigned flight, shape defaults
and palette behavior. These components also reach nested charged rockets
through the shared converter. Projectile entity simulation and visible
Java/native comparisons remain separate requirements.

Translate typed display.Lore entries into ordered standard Java lore components.
Preserve blank and wrong-typed members, and split embedded LF after parsing
formatting so styles carry across lines but reset to native purple/italic at
each entry. Authoritative lore replaces mapping diagnostics without changing
stored native item data. Rawtext localization and complete native hover context
remain separate requirements.

Official BDS 1.26.51.1 build 51061372/protocol 2193 supplies the retained lore
in a controlled placed chest, but the previous Java component is empty.
Bounded execution of the matching native item assembler confirms per-member
StringTag defaults, LF boundaries and per-entry style. Java network roundtrip
and style tests verify the standard fallback; native UI pixels remain unverified.

Resolve Bedrock rawtext item lore, including translated parameters and newlines. Target Geyser 26_50/Potion mappings confirm trial potion metadata 43-46 and tipped-arrow metadata 44-47; preserve these effect components and ominous bottle amplifier 0-4. Known stew/star auxiliary ranges retain native identity and server-applied behavior without fabricated effect durations. Tests exercise shipped mappings, rawtext and bottle bounds.
